+++ b/releasenotes/notes/answer-builder-validate-reference-pattern-3c9f5a1d7b2e4f60.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    ``AnswerBuilder`` now validates ``reference_pattern`` in ``run()`` and raises a clear ``ValueError`` if the
+    effective pattern, either set at initialization or overridden in ``run()``, does not contain exactly one capture
+    group. Previously such a pattern was accepted and only failed when a reply contained a matching reference, with a
+    cryptic ``int()`` error like ``invalid literal for int() with base 10: '[1]'``.
